<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia s/adj Oct employment rose 25,500.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia s/adj Oct employment rose 25,500.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's seasonally adjusted estimate of the number of employed persons rose 25,500 in October to 8.37 million, against 8.35 million in September and 8.24 million a year earlier, the Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>The seasonally adjusted unemployment rate rose to 8.8 percent in October from 8.7 percent in September, compared with 8.6 percent in October 1995.</p>
<p>Economists had on average expected employment to rise around 12,000 in October, seasonally-adjusted, with the unemployment rate steady at 8.7 percent.  </p>
<p>AUSTRALIAN UNEMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>    (Seasonally adj)	 Oct 96     Sept 96	Oct 95</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate     8.8 pct     8.7 pct	8.6 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		 8.37 million    8.35 million     8.24 million</p>
<p>    Unemployed		806,900     799,100	780,300</p>
<p>    Participation Rate   63.6 pct    63.5 pct     63.6 pct</p>
<p>(Unadjusted)</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate     8.4 pct     8.7 pct	8.2 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		 8.39 million    8.43 million     8.26 million</p>
<p>    Unemployed		764,900     800,200	738,900</p>
<p>    Participation Rate   63.5 pct    64.1 pct     63.4 pct</p>
<p>(Trend Estimates)</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate    8.7 pct	8.7 pct	8.4 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		8.37 million     8.37 million     8.29 million</p>
<p>    Unemployed	     801,500	796,200	763,400</p>
<p>    Participation Rate  63.6 pct     63.6 pct     63.8 pct</p>
<p>The Bureau said part-time employment rose around 15,800 in October, while full-time employment rose around 9,800.</p>
<p>It said female employment in October rose by 27,500.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
